# `allocator : AllocatorKind.Debug` (plans/backlog/ZIG_ADOPTION_CANDIDATES.md
# Z11) reaches the child compile as `--allocator debug`. The clean probe's
# report counts no live block; the leaking probe's run fails the build with
# the leak check's verdict. The "Building" lines name the host binary (`.exe`
# on Windows) and the report's peak moves with the runtime, so only the counts
# and the verdict are kept.
stdout_keep_match=(probe: .*|live at exit: [0-9]+ blocks / [0-9]+ bytes|leak check failed: [0-9]+ blocks / [0-9]+ bytes|exit status [0-9]+)
timeout=900
